            {
                "box": {
                    "hidden": 1,
                    "id": "obj-4",
                    "maxclass": "newobj",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patcher": {
                        "fileversion": 1,
                        "appversion": {
                            "major": 9,
                            "minor": 1,
                            "revision": 3,
                            "architecture": "x64",
                            "modernui": 1
                        },
                        "classnamespace": "box",
                        "rect": [ 1933.0, 156.0, 482.0, 875.0 ],
                        "boxes": [
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "id": "obj-3",
                                    "linecount": 50,
                                    "maxclass": "comment",
                                    "numinlets": 1,
                                    "numoutlets": 0,
                                    "patching_rect": [ 12.0, 47.0, 459.0, 690.0 ],
                                    "text": "D E S C R I P T I O N :\n\nThis snippet can save and recall multiple \nscenes / states / presets of the entire patch\n\nYou can write (and later read) a file with the saved scenes on your disk, this works also without MAX license!\n\nthe scenes file is saved in the patch folder, if the patch is not yet saved, it'll get saved in the last location max was navigated into \n\n\nU S A G E :\n\nWhen you want to save the status of your patch (scene) \nshift+click on a square slot, there are 20 slots\nto recall the scene just click on its slot\nshift+option+click to delete it\n\nyou can also recall the preset via float number box (left) and you can also interpolate between scenes through decimal values\n\nTo insert a scene in between others or remove it and automagically get the other slots to shift position you can do it vai number box and umenu on the right\n\nTo save your scene collection to disk write a name on the blue text box and choose write in the umenu\n\nto read it back its the same procedure but choose read in teh umenu\n\n\nI M P O R T A N T ! ! !\n\nBoth for the insert/remove and write/read the action happens immediately when choosing the umenu option\n\nRecalling all values of all parameters of the whole patch is a big complicated and messy process, it can happen that things do not get recalled in the optimal order of events, but fear not! if this happens you'll just need to trigger the scene recall again and all should fall in the right place\n\nthe green toggle \"recall_first_after_file_read\" lets you choose if when loading a scenes collection file the first scene is triggered automatically, or not (on by default)\n\nif for some reason the file writing and reading does not work, you can write and read via system dialog\n\nstoragewindow gives you an overview on the stored scenes and all saved values \n\n\n"
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "box": {
                                    "comment": "",
                                    "id": "obj-1",
                                    "index": 1,
                                    "maxclass": "inlet",
                                    "numinlets": 0,
                                    "numoutlets": 1,
                                    "outlettype": [ "" ],
                                    "patching_rect": [ 11.0, 8.0, 30.0, 30.0 ]
                                }
                            }
                        ],
                        "lines": []
                    },
                    "patching_rect": [ 21.0, 233.5, 77.0, 22.0 ],
                    "text": "p description"
                }
